## Two natural continuations

G3CI differentiates the exact 100-term G3CA polynomial

```text
u v P_delta (t0 t1 t2) C_section
```

through the affine H02 chart and its recursive H11 return. Its H02 quotient at
the terminal fiber agrees exactly with G3CC. The full rational reduction,
however, also has `920` nonzero H11 anchor entries. It is therefore not the
same affine source used by G3CD, which is placed purely in the associated
graded H02 slot.

The canonical associated-graded continuation retains the varying H02 quotient
and projects away every recursive H11 component. This version anchors G3CD
with zero residual and is the natural continuation at the tier declared by
G3CA, G3CC and G3CD.

## Riccati decision

The full raw-polynomial jet differs from the unique G3CH target in `1,145`
entries. More decisively, the correctly anchored associated-graded H02 jet
differs in `1,139` entries. Therefore the current selected source rule fails a
necessary first-order condition for the 249-dimensional Schur-Riccati
transport at the terminal good fiber.

An engineered non-graded source-section lift could be chosen to match the
G3CH jet; this result does not rule that out. Such a lift would need an
independent MTT selection theorem. Choosing it because it repairs the Riccati
identity would be circular.

Absent that new theorem, the legitimate continuation remains the full
1,509-dimensional inhomogeneous system, equivalently its 1,510-dimensional
homogeneous affine lift. The static 249-square Schur packet remains valid for
rank, obstruction and preconditioning uses only.

